A||||4||DaveL||Quick Headlight Rebuild Question||||6||
Z||000000||DaveL||08-12-2001||10:38 AM||||The right headlight on my 87 SE suddenly started struggling to get up, taking a few bumps until the gear finally caught. Got Rodney Dickman's rebuild kit and have the drivers side headlight assembly off. Looks like it's gonna be pretty easy. The instructions say that the passenger side drive gear has some sort of ridge, and prescribes filing the ridge off 5 teeth of the gear before reassembly.<P>What's the scoop with this? I wanna finish this headlight job today because it really sucks when you can't get one up .||||reg||6
Z||000001||Songman||08-12-2001||10:50 AM||||Dave, it's pretty easy once you get it apart and have the parts in front of you. The passenger side is a little more difficult than the driver's side because the motor is built backwards. You just have to make that little modification for clearance. You'll see it easily enough. I jumped into mine with no idea what to expect and had both of them done and back on the car in an hour. Well worth the time and effort. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-12-2001||02:28 PM||||Warning! If the output shaft binds coming out, Do Not force it. Clean off all trash and file off any rased spot on the shoulders where the arm bolts down. If you force the shaft out You Will Damage the bearing and dust seal.<P>There are 2 choices.<P>Do the drivers side first.<BR>Look at the gear.<BR>See the "rim" around one side of the teeth? that rim gets filed when you do the passengers side.<P>You can get the pasenger side out but not in without filing the rim.<P>You other choice... is to pull the motor shaft from the passenger side. Then you don't need to file the big gear to get it back in place.<P>lube the big gear, washers, and output shaft good with White grease.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-12-2001||03:56 PM||||That's right, Ogre. I had never heard that but just luckily pulled my driver's side first. Seeing how the thing worked certainly made it easier to figure out the directions for the passenger side.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaveL||08-13-2001||09:10 AM||||Got it done. I see what the deal is with the ridge now. Was able to force it in and out without any filing, and it works great. It did take a few adjustments of motor height to get the drivers side to work. It was way too high and would only open partially untill I lowered it. Thanks for the replies!||||reg||10
